{
  "title": "Osteonecrosis of the Knee",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/knee-and-sports/3025/osteonecrosis-of-the-knee",
  "subtitle": "Updated: May 31 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Osteonecrosis of the knee represents a condition caused by reduced blood flow to bone secondary to a variety of risk factors such as sickle cell disease, steroid use, alcoholism, autoimmune disorders, and hypercoagulable states.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is radiographic for advanced disease but requires MRI for detection of early or subclinical disease.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is generally observation with management of the underlying systemic condition. Operative management is indicated for advanced disease with presence of severe subchondral collapse.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographic",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "women:men 3:1",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "more common in women <55 years with risk factors",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "reported to be found after knee arthroscopy in middle-aged women",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "typically involves more than one compartment of the knee or even the metaphysis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "80% are bilateral",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "multifocal lesions are not uncommon",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**alcoholism**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "dysbaric disorders (decompression sickness, \"the bends\")",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "marrow-replacing diseases (e.g. Gaucher's disease)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**sickle cell disease**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**hypercoagulable states**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**steroids** (either endogenous or exogenous)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "SLE",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "inflammatory bowel disease",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "transplant patient",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "virus (CMV, hepatitis, HIV, rubella, rubeola, varicella)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "protease inhibitors (type of HIV medication)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**trauma**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "spontaneous osteonecrosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "appears to represent a subchondral insufficiency fracture",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "another hypothesis is an association with a meniscal root tear",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Physical Exam",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain with weightbearing, especially sitting to standing",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "first line imaging studies",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP knee",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "lateral knee",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "merchant view knee",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "wedge-shaped lesion on imaging",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most useful study",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**highest sensitivity and specificity**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "T1: dark",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**T2: bright (marrow edema)**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Osteochondritis dissecans** (OCD)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "more commonly found at lateral aspect of medial femoral condyle of 15 to 20-year-old males",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Transient osteoporosis**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "more common in young to middle-aged men",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "multiple joint involvement found in 40% of patients (transient migratory osteoporosis)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Occult fractures and bone bruises**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "associated with trauma, weak bones, or overuse",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Spontaneous osteonecrosis of the knee (SONK)**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "NSAIDs, limited weightbearing, quadriceps strengthening, activity modification",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**indications**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**first-line of treatment**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**outcomes**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**favorable, but less so than nonoperative management for SONK**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "diagnostic arthroscopy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**indications**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**remove small, unstable fragments from the joint**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**core decompression**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**indications**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**extra-articular lesions**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**osteochondral allograft**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**indications**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**large symptomatic lesions in younger patients that failed nonoperative management**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "total knee arthroplasty (TKA)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3025/images/img_2964..jpg",
                  "caption": "Image of a knee during a total knee arthroplasty with lateral femoral condyle collapse due to osteonecrosis of the knee. The lateral side of the knee is closer to the camera"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**indications**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**large area of involvement**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**collapse**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**osteonecrosis in multiple compartments**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Self-limiting condition",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
